  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) and model overestimates prices.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks after sharp spikes — model tends to overshoot and overreact to recent highs.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if price deviates > ±10% from 5-day moving average, adjust forecast toward historical mean.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0.00) — model underreacts to bullish signals.",
    "For horizon > 15 days, reduce forecast volatility — model overfits short-term noise and fails to smooth long-term trends.",
    "When sentiment is positive and price is trending down, apply a downward bias correction to prevent model from overcorrecting."
  ]
}
